[{"name":"UnityCatalog 0.6.0","uuid":"373899911","tag_name":"v0.6.0","target_commitish":"main","body":"We are thrilled to announce **Unity Catalog 0.6.0** release, which includes exciting new features, many bug fixes, and improvements. A huge thank you to the awesome community who made this release possible!\r\n\r\n## Artifacts in this release\r\n\r\n* Maven artifacts:\r\n  * [unitycatalog-server](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-server/versions), [unitycatalog-client](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-client/versions), [unitycatalog-hadoop](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-hadoop/versions)\r\n  * [unitycatalog-spark_4.0_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.0_2.13/versions) for Apache Spark 4.0.x\r\n  * [unitycatalog-spark_4.1_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.1_2.13/versions) for Apache Spark 4.1.x\r\n  * [unitycatalog-spark_4.2_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.2_2.13/versions) for Apache Spark 4.2.x — **new in 0.6.0**\r\n* PyPI: [unitycatalog-client](https://pypi.org/project/unitycatalog-client/)\r\n* Docker: [unitycatalog](https://hub.docker.com/r/unitycatalog/unitycatalog/tags) (v0.6.0)\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n### UC Spark Connector: Apache Spark 4.2 Support\r\n\r\nUnity Catalog 0.6.0 adds a connector artifact for **Apache Spark 4.2.x**, alongside the existing Spark 4.0.x and 4.1.x artifacts. This is the artifact that unlocks the view and metric-view DDL described below.\r\n\r\n| Spark Versions | UC Spark connector artifact |\r\n| :---- | :---- |\r\n| Apache Spark 4.0.x | [unitycatalog-spark_4.0_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.0_2.13/versions) |\r\n| Apache Spark 4.1.x | [unitycatalog-spark_4.1_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.1_2.13/versions) |\r\n| Apache Spark 4.2.x | [unitycatalog-spark_4.2_2.13](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/io.unitycatalog/unitycatalog-spark_4.2_2.13/versions) |\r\n\r\nTo initialize a Spark session for **Spark 4.2.x**, use the following command:\r\n\r\n```shell\r\nexport CATALOG_NAME=unity\r\nexport UC_URI=http://localhost:8080\r\nexport UC_TOKEN=\u003cuc-token\u003e\r\n\r\nbin/spark-sql --name \"unity-spark42\" \\\r\n   --master \"local[*]\" \\\r\n   --packages \"org.apache.hadoop:hadoop-aws:3.4.2,io.delta:delta-spark_4.2_2.13:4.4.0,io.unitycatalog:unitycatalog-spark_4.2_2.13:0.6.0\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.extensions=io.delta.sql.DeltaSparkSessionExtension\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.catalog.spark_catalog=org.apache.spark.sql.delta.catalog.DeltaCatalog\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.hadoop.fs.s3.impl=org.apache.hadoop.fs.s3a.S3AFileSystem\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.catalog.$CATALOG_NAME=io.unitycatalog.spark.UCSingleCatalog\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.catalog.$CATALOG_NAME.uri=$UC_URI\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.catalog.$CATALOG_NAME.token=$UC_TOKEN\" \\\r\n   --conf \"spark.sql.defaultCatalog=$CATALOG_NAME\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor other Spark versions, use the same command with the matching `--packages` coordinates:\r\n\r\n* **Spark 4.0.x**: `org.apache.hadoop:hadoop-aws:3.4.1,io.delta:delta-spark_4.0_2.13:4.4.0,io.unitycatalog:unitycatalog-spark_4.0_2.13:0.6.0`\r\n* **Spark 4.1.x**: `org.apache.hadoop:hadoop-aws:3.4.2,io.delta:delta-spark_4.1_2.13:4.4.0,io.unitycatalog:unitycatalog-spark_4.1_2.13:0.6.0`\r\n\r\n**NOTICE**: the UC Spark connector 0.6.0 works with Delta Lake 4.4.0, and uses the UC Delta API to access UC managed tables by default.\r\n\r\n### Metric Views: End-to-End Support, from SQL to Catalog\r\n\r\nMetric views give you a governed semantic layer: define reusable named aggregations (**measures**) and the columns used to slice them (**dimensions**) once in Unity Catalog, and every consumer computes them from the same definition instead of hand-writing the aggregation in each query.\r\n\r\nUnity Catalog 0.5.0 introduced the catalog side of this as an experimental preview — the server could store and serve metric views. 0.6.0 now fully supports metric views with **Apache Spark 4.2**: you define them in SQL, query their measures in SQL, and Unity Catalog governs them like any other object.\r\n\r\n### SQL Views: A New First-Class Catalog Object\r\n\r\nUnity Catalog 0.6.0 also adds **SQL views** (VIEW) as a catalog object. A view is a named, governed SQL query: the server stores the view's SQL text, its column list, and the tables it reads from, so any engine can discover and resolve it through the standard `/tables` API surface.\r\n\r\n**Engine support: read on Spark 4.0 / 4.1, create on Spark 4.2.** Creating a view requires Spark's v2 view-catalog API, which landed in Spark 4.2. On Spark 4.0 and 4.1 the connector cannot create, replace, rename, or drop a view — but it can **read** one:\r\n\r\n| Capability | Spark 4.0 / 4.1 | Spark 4.2 |\r\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\r\n| CREATE VIEW, DROP VIEW | not supported | supported |\r\n| SELECT, DESCRIBE | supported | supported |\r\n| Listing | via SHOW TABLES | via SHOW VIEWS and SHOW TABLES |\r\n\r\nReplacing a view (CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW) and renaming one (ALTER VIEW ... RENAME TO) are not supported yet on any version.\r\n\r\n### UC Delta API: Delete, Rename, Exists Endpoints, and Safe Commit Retries\r\n\r\nThe [UC Delta API](https://github.com/unitycatalog/unitycatalog/tree/main/api/delta-docs) introduced in 0.5.0 gains the remaining table-lifecycle operations, so a Delta engine can now operate catalog-managed Delta tables through one REST surface.\r\n\r\n### Security Hardening\r\n\r\nThis release includes several hardening fixes in credential vending and authorization. All are server-side; no configuration change is required.\r\n\r\n### UC Server: Authentication and Authorization Improvements\r\n\r\n**Wildcard issuer and audience allowlists.** `server.allowed-issuers` and `server.audiences` now accept `*` as a single-DNS-label wildcard, which makes multi-tenant deployments practical without enumerating every tenant host.\r\n\r\n**Configurable access token lifetime.** UC access tokens issued by the `/auth/tokens` token exchange now carry an expiration, configurable via `server.access-token-timeout` (default `PT24H`), with the lifetime reported back to clients in the response's `expires_in` field. See the breaking-change notice below.\r\n\r\n**Configurable OAuth scope.** The client-credentials OAuth flow previously hardcoded `scope=all-apis`, which is correct for the UC/Databricks token endpoint but invalid for other identity providers. You can now set the scope explicitly.\r\n\r\n### Engine and Runtime Upgrades\r\n\r\n* **Apache Iceberg 1.11.0** (from 1.9.2).\r\n* **Apache Spark 4.2.0** support in the connector, alongside the existing 4.0.x and 4.1.x lines.\r\n\r\n### Notable Bug Fixes\r\n\r\n* **PostgreSQL support for managed Delta tables**: the server could not work with PostgreSQL because of an incompatible column definition.\r\n* **No more hanging requests on empty responses**: a response with no body — such as the Iceberg HEAD endpoint — previously may have hung forever.\r\n* **Metastore-wide model listing pagination fixed**: GET /models without a catalog or schema returned an invalid page token.\r\n\r\n## Breaking Changes and Migration Notes\r\n\r\n**UC access tokens now expire.** Before 0.6.0, UC access tokens issued by the `/auth/tokens` token exchange had no expiration and were valid indefinitely. Starting with 0.6.0 they expire after `server.access-token-timeout`, which defaults to **24 hours**.\r\n\r\n* Clients must re-exchange (or refresh, using the `expires_in` value now returned by `/auth/tokens`) at least once per day under the default setting.\r\n* Deployments that relied on non-expiring tokens should set a longer duration explicitly during migration:\r\n\r\n```\r\nserver.access-token-timeout=PT720H\r\n```\r\n\r\n* On Helm, the same value is available as `auth.accessTokenTimeout`.\r\n* This applies **only** to access tokens from the token exchange. The bootstrap admin token in `etc/conf/token.txt` is a service token and is unchanged — it still does not expire.\r\n\r\n## Full Changes\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/unitycatalog/unitycatalog/compare/v0.5.1...v0.6.0\r\n\r\n## Contributors\r\n\r\nThanks to everyone who contributed to this release:\r\n\r\nAnas Khan, Bhavya Joshi, Chen Wang, Matt Van Horn, Murali Ramanujam, Scott Haines, Simon Maling, Thomas Wiest, Timothy Wang, Yi Li, Yuya Ebihara, foss-contributor, openinx, seewishnew, SreeramaYeshwanthGowd, tiennguyen-onehouse","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"immutable":false,"published_at":"2026-08-20T17:10:08.000Z","created_at":"2026-09-08T01:06:13.482Z","author":"yili-db","assets":[],"last_synced_at":"2026-09-08T01:06:12.873Z","html_url":"https://github.com/unitycatalog/unitycatalog/releases/tag/v0.6.0","release_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/hosts/GitHub/repositories/unitycatalog%2Funitycatalog/releases/v0.6.0","tag_url":"https://repos.ecosyste.ms/api/v1/hosts/GitHub/repositories/unitycatalog%2Funitycatalog/tags/v0.6.0"}]